      "Language": "hrv",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERB) is one from the most frequent disease of the upper gastrointestinal system. Extraesophageal manifestations GERB occur most often as lung manifestations, ORL discomforts, and as noncardial pain in breasts. GERB is associated with the various respiratory diseases and symptoms as are the bronchial asthma, cough, wheezing. The episodes of the sour reflux into the esophagus, specially in children, can provoke the symptoms discapper mainly in all patients who have used the antisecretoral therapy."},
